{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> Know that the first three plagues were by the hand of Aaron, and the signs were in the lowly things, as I explained above, for two were in the waters and the third in the dust of the earth. And the plagues that were by Moses' hand with the staff were in the upper things, just as his rank is higher than Aaron's rank — like the plague of hail and the locusts, which the wind brought, and the darkness, which was in the air. Also the plague of boils was by his hand, only three were without the staff: ערוב (mixed wild beasts), דבר (pestilence), and מכת בכורים (the plague of the firstborn). And one without the staff was by the hand of Moses with slight participation by Aaron, and that is the plague of boils." "The sense of והיה לכנים (and it became lice) is like והיה לאבק (and it became dust) (below, v. 9): as though from the dust that Aaron strikes, there shall rise and generate lice in all the land of Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:39.298996869Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}